# Generated by Phase: IMPLEMENT | Feature: EVOL-059
"""The lens canary (EVOL-059): calibration under model drift.

The framework keeps model ALIASES; the id behind an alias moves. As soon as a lens is known to have run on a moved
model (its first real round on it tells the id), it reviews THIS before its next real work: one synthetic diff of a synthetic project with two planted defects per lens and the
expected findings — security (a read without the tenant predicate, a planted credential), correctness (a dishonest
test, a contract ↔ DTO mismatch), governance (an artefact without its manifest entry, a manifest changelog without
its bump), fidelity (a specified scenario with no test, a mock state no code implements). Nothing here comes from a
real project.

fixture     the diff, stored base64 AT REST so that no scanner and no regex floor sees the planted credential in the
            repository (a literal scanner; one that decodes base64 is not fooled, and need not be — the credential is
            invented); decoded only into the critic's scratch input OUTSIDE the tree, where the planted line itself
            carries the `canary-secret` marker. `gate.py canary --fixture` prints it, writes nothing.
expected    per lens: id, what, and the locations a finding may anchor at (file, line in the NEW file).
judge       `--judge --lens L --model ID < return.md`: a planted defect is FOUND when the return carries a finding on
            one of its files (the path's tail), within `agents.canary.line_tolerance` lines of the anchor in the NEW
            file's numbering or in the diff text's own (a critic counts either way; the filler leading the diff keeps
            the two spaces apart), at a severity above informational; the verdict (found, missed) and the model are
            recorded under `judged` in .claude/state/canary.json; red when any planted defect was missed; a return
            with no finding in the contract shape and no `no findings` line is a fault, not a verdict.
seen        `--seen --lens L --model ID`: the model a lens last ran a real round on (from its return's `Model:` line).
plan        `--plan [--all]`: the lenses owed a canary — the model a lens last ran on differs from the one it was last
            judged on, it was never judged, or the id is `unknown`; `--all` owes every lens (on demand). The id is known from a return, so
            a lens's first real round on a moved model runs before the canary owes it — the canary follows that round.
            A red canary never blocks the train: it opens the review of the spawn policy by RDR with the user.
"""
